WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
I wanted to ask you some more about LSU.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:08.240
You were at LSU during the [Huey P.] Long years, I mean, when he was pumping a lot of money into the university.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:08.960
What was it like?

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.740
Did you go to any of the football games where he had the trains and, you know, paid . . . ?

5
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.860
Well, that was only one occasion.

6
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.080
He’d come out and try to lead the band, which was liked by some and despised by others.

7
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:28.480
And of course he hired [Colonel Lawrence] “Biff” Jones, who was an army major, and got him to start coaching LSU.

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:40.320
And Jones was an excellent recruiter, and Huey helped, and they started getting players from all over the United States: Texas, Colorado, New Mexico.

9
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.360
And he brought those boys in here.

10
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:50.440
And LSU was creeping up in notoriety in the football annals throughout the United States.

11
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:56.940
And then Huey got to the point . . . And I’m talking generally now, because that’s all I know of.

12
00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:03.000
He wanted to start coaching the football team and he wanted to . . . Of course you probably know that, or know of it.

13
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.500
And he wanted to send in players and he wanted to substitute and all that.

14
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.840
And Jones just wouldn’t take it, and so Jones resigned.

15
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.280
He got transferred.

16
00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:19.060
He was in the army, and he had the army transfer him, I believe, to some Midwestern state.

17
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:30.120
Kansas, or . . . I think it was some Kansas . . . He went and he coached up there ’til his death. [Jones went on to coach at the Universities of Oklahoma and Nebraska] But Jones was a very fine man and a hell of a good football coach.
